  "worked_solution": "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ 3|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
